; adversarial test: exists-elim (`pick`) must reject a conclusion that mentions a
; fresh constant introduced *inside* the block that isn't the witness itself -- `helper`
; here is a bystander declared inside `pick`'s block; letting it leak into the
; conclusion would mean the "proof" secretly depends on a name that stops existing the
; moment the block closes. See doc/kurt-soundness.md, and
; forall-intro-rejects-leaked-constant.kurt for the `let` counterpart.
;
; note: like that file, this can't use `expect` -- the failure happens while *closing*
; the `pick` block, while the mode is still `pick`, not `expect`.
load logic
bool Q, P
arity Q 1
arity P 1
use exists x Q x
pick y with Q y
    const helper
    use P helper
    P helper
true
;;; ProofError: the line (its conclusion) of the `pick` block may not contain constant symbols
